## Phase 1 — Discovery
- NOTE: export.arxiv.org API was persistently rate-limited (HTTP 429 "Rate exceeded") for the
  entire session — likely an IP-level ban carried over from earlier launchd invocations. Retried
  after 30s/90s/150s cooldowns; all returned 429. Semantic Scholar Graph API also 429.
- websearch intentionally NOT used as the primary discovery source: yesterday's run (2026-09-07)
  documented that websearch FABRICATES arxiv IDs (flagged "xxxxx" placeholders). System also
  limits websearch to one call per message. So websearch is unreliable for verified paper IDs.
- FELL BACK to arXiv RSS feeds (http://export.arxiv.org/rss/<cat>) — a DIFFERENT endpoint on the
  same host that was NOT rate-limited (HTTP 200 for all 5 categories). RSS returns the freshest
  submissions per category with REAL arxiv IDs + full abstracts (in <content:encoded>).
- Fetched RSS for: cs.CV (174 items), cs.LG (228), cs.CL (151), cs.DC (20), cs.GR (8).
- Filtered per direction by keyword match against title+abstract. All items below are arXiv-RSS-
  verified (real IDs resolving to the stated titles + abstracts).
- Also tested OpenAlex API (api.openalex.org, different host, HTTP 200) as a secondary source;
  used title_and_abstract.search but signal-to-noise was poor (journal articles, sparse abstracts).
  Kept arXiv RSS as primary due to superior relevance + recency.

